-- Demonstrates CatMLM's new "inter-associations"/"inter-constraints"
-- sections (2026-09-01), added specifically because bookshop_corrected.pl
-- -- a Prolog description of a real 3-level MLM model -- had one fact
-- CatMLM previously had no syntax for at all:
--
--   association(catShop,_,classes([[catalog,'Catalog'],1,catalog],
--                                  [[bookShop,'BookShop'],*,bookShop])).
--
-- an association crossing two levels directly, with no route through
-- the clabject/category mechanism (a "catalog" is not itself instantiated
-- by anything below it; it's linked to a "bookShop" directly). This file
-- is that fact's translation, plus one inter-constraint exercising the
-- resulting cross-level role.
--
-- Two levels, standing in for bookshop_corrected.pl's 'Catalog' and
-- 'BookShop': "catalog" is a category one level below could instantiate
-- (it isn't, here, to keep this example minimal), and "bookShop" is an
-- ordinary class at the level below. Every reference inside
-- inter-associations/inter-constraints must be Model@Class -- bare names
-- are rejected exactly as they already are in plain MLM-USE.

MLM InterAssocBookshopBridge

model Catalog < NONE
category catalog
end
category book
end

model BookShop < Catalog
category bookShop
end
clabject bookCopy : book
end

inter-associations
association catShop between
Catalog@catalog[1] role catalog
BookShop@bookShop[*] role bookShop
end

inter-constraints
context Catalog@catalog inv NonEmptyCatalog:
self.bookShop->notEmpty()
